In the middle of it, a question got asked out loud that changed the shape of the fight entirely: not whether these things had been summoned, but whether they had ever been anything else. Three fingers to a claw. Three fingers on every set of remains they'd find later. The barrier here was thin enough to let things cross on their own — nobody had needed to call them. And if nobody had called them, then whoever this had happened to hadn't been taken away from this fight. They were standing in it.

